```text
Page 2 of 6
4842-7393-4218v2
Dyno Nobel and Dyno Nobel would not purchase Parcel A if not for that promise.
Therefore, if Dyno Nobel purchases Parcel A in accordance with this Agreement, the City
will be obligated to pay Dyno Nobel $117,500.00 and convey Parcel B to Dyno Nobel in
accordance with this Agreement.

2. At closing, and subject to the terms and conditions set forth in Paragraphs 3-17:

a. Dyno Nobel shall issue certified funds payable to Mariah in the amount of $1,295,000.00
for Parcel A, which certified funds shall be accepted by Mariah as full and final payment
of consideration for the purchase of Parcel A; and

b. Mariah shall execute and deliver to the City a general warranty deed conveying to the City
all of Mariah’s right, title and interest in Parcel A and showing no additional exceptions to
those permitted in Paragraphs 3 and 4, and furnish tax statements or certificates to Dyno
Nobel and the City showing no delinquent taxes on Parcel A; and

c. Simultaneously with the conveyance of title by Mariah of Parcel A to the City, the City
shall issue certified funds payable to Dyno Nobel in the amount of $117,500.00 and shall
execute and deliver a special warranty deed conveying to Dyno Nobel all of the City’s
right, title and interest in Parcel B, and showing no additional exceptions to those permitted
in Section 4, and furnish tax statements or certificates to Dyno Nobel showing no
delinquent taxes on Parcel B.

3. Mariah reserves an undivided Forty-Nine Percent (49%) interest in the Mineral Estate.  Dyno
Nobel does not reserve and retain any of the Mineral Estate, and Parcel A shall be conveyed
by Mariah to the City subject to Mariah’s reserved Forty-Nine Percent (49%) interest of the
Mineral Estate.  “Mineral Estate” means all oil, gas, and other minerals in and under and that
may be produced from Parcel A, any royalty under any existing or future mineral lease
covering any part of Parcel A, executive rights (including the right to sign a mineral lease
covering any part of Parcel A), implied rights of ingress and egress, exploration and
development rights, production and drilling rights, mineral lease payments, and all related
rights and benefits. The Mineral Estate does NOT include water, sand, gravel, limestone,
building stone, caliche, surface shale, near-surface lignite, and iron, but DOES include the
reasonable use of these surface materials for mining, drilling, exploring, operating, developing,
or removing the oil, gas, and other minerals from Parcel A.

4. Mariah certifies it has provided to the City and Dyno Nobel all surveys or plats of or which
include Parcel A, all documents in its possession or control relating to environmental matters,
including but not limited to a Phase 1 Environmental Assessment, any geotechnical surveys or
reports, water rights, and minerals. The City certifies it has provided to Dyno Nobel any
surveys or plats of or which include Parcel B, all documents in its possession or control relating
to environmental matters, including but not limited to a Phase 1 Environmental Assessment,
any geotechnical surveys or reports, water rights, and minerals. Before closing, the City and
