### Page 3 of 6

```text
Page 3 of 6
4842-7393-4218v2
Dyno Nobel, may terminate this Agreement for any reason or no reason.  Before closing, the
City and Dyno Nobel may conduct inspections, surveys and studies of the Parcels as each
deems necessary or appropriate to inspect or evaluate the Parcel that it will be receiving at
closing.  The City’s and Dyno Nobel’s physical inspection of Parcel A and Parcel B, as
appropriate, may include soils and geotechnical assessments and an ASTM Phase 1, or
equivalent environmental due diligence investigation, to determine or confirm the condition of
the respective Parcel. The parties will reasonably agree to extend the  closing period if
additional time is needed to complete a Phase 1 or other environmental assessments.

5. The City shall pay the premium for a standard form minimum value title insurance policy
issued byTown Square Title of Wyoming, LLC, Cheyenne, Wyoming, (“Title Company”) to
insure the City’s title to Parcel A.  Dyno Nobel will pay the premium for a standard form title
insurance policy (or extended coverage and any endorsements, as required by Dyno Nobel)
issued by Title Company to insure Dyno Nobel’s title to Parcel B.  Title to be conveyed, in
each instance, shall be good and marketable, subject only to liens, encumbrances, restrictions,
easements and other burdens which are not objected to in writing within 15 days after the City’s
receipt of a commitment for the issuance of a title insurance policy for Parcel A or within 15
days after Dyno Nobel’s receipt of a commitment for the issuance of a title insurance policy
for Parcel B.  In the event any exception shown on the title commitment for Parcel A and
objected to by the City is not cured by Mariah before closing, the City and/or Dyno Nobel shall
each have the right, in either’s sole discretion, to cancel this Agreement.  In the event any
exception shown on the title commitment for Parcel B and objected to by Dyno Nobel is not
cured by the City before closing, Dyno Nobel shall have the right, in its sole discretion, to
cancel this Agreement.  Closing shall occur when Title Company, is in a position to record all
documents required under this Agreement, to make all disbursements, and to issue the title
insurance policies provided for herein, but in no event later than 20 days after the Effective
Date of this Agreement, unless extended in writing by mutual agreement of the parties.

6. If, at the time of transfer of title, either Parcel A or Parcel B, or any part of either parcel, is
subject to an assessment or assessments payable in installments, all such installments not due
or delinquent at the time of transfer shall nevertheless be deemed to be due and payable at such
time, and all such assessments shall be paid and discharged by Mariah with respect to Parcel
A and by the City with respect to Parcel B prior to closing.

7. Each party will be responsible for its attorneys’ fees, costs, and expenses associated with this
Agreement. The escrow agent’s escrow fees shall be divided between Mariah and Dyno Nobel.
The City shall pay any and all fees associated with recording fees necessary to record
instruments received by the City at closing and Dyno Nobel shall be responsible for any and
all fees associated with recording the special warranty deed to be delivered by the City at
closing with respect to Parcel B. Any other closing costs will be divided amongst the parties
as customarily done in Cheyenne, Wyoming.

8. Risk of loss or damage by fire or other casualty to either Parcel A or Parcel B, or any part of
either parcel, prior to closing shall be the risk of the current owner thereof.  In the event of
```

