9. To Mariah’s knowledge, all existing uses of Parcel A are lawful and in compliance with all
federal, state, and municipal laws and ordinances, including ordinances relating to
environmental protection and zoning.  It is mutually understood and agreed that Mariah has
been making use of Parcel A.  For this reason, Dyno Nobel and the City each expressly
disclaim any warranties that all existing uses of Parcel A are lawful or in compliance with all
federal, state, and municipal laws and ordinances, including ordinances related to
environmental protection and zoning.  Mariah warrants and represents that it has no
knowledge of any fact or circumstance that would preclude the use of Parcel A for the purposes
of outdoor recreation, wind energy development or other municipal purposes. To the City’s
knowledge all existing uses of Parcel B are lawful and in compliance with all federal, state,
and municipal laws and ordinances, including ordinances relating to environmental protection
and zoning. Dyno Nobel expressly disclaims any warranties that all existing uses of Parcel B
are lawful or in compliance with all federal, state, and municipal laws and ordinances,
including ordinances related to environmental protection and zoning. The City and Dyno Nobel
have received copies of the appraisal report for Parcels A and B prepared by Accuvalue, LLC
and have knowledge of the contents thereof.

10.  The parties mutually warrant and represent that no brokers or agents other than Hayden
Outdoors, L.L.C., 501 Main St., Windsor, CO 80550, (“Seller’s Agent”) have been employed
or retained by any party in connection with the negotiation or consummation of the purchase
and land exchange contemplated by this Agreement and thatMariah shall pay all Seller’s
Agent’s fees, commission or other compensation or reimbursement for expenses made by
Seller’s Agent in connection with this Agreement or the transactions it contemplates.  Neither
the City nor Dyno Nobel  shall become obligated to pay any commission of any kind or nature
to any broker or agent upon the closing of this purchase.

11. All notices required by this Agreement shall be in writing and shall be served on the parties at
their addresses, as indicated above, or on their attorneys at their business addresses.  The
mailing of a notice by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested, shall serve as
sufficient notice.  Notices may also be served by personal delivery.  Notices may also be
served by e-mail, or by the use of a facsimile machine, so long as a copy of the notice sent by
e-mail or a copy of the notice sent by facsimile, with proof of e-mail or facsimile transmission,
is also sent by regular mail on the date of transmission.

12. This Agreement shall not be binding upon the City until such time as this Agreement has been
approved by the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne.  Except as provided herein, this
Agreement, and the covenants and conditions herein, shall bind and inure to the benefit of the
parties, and their respective heirs, personal representatives, successors and assigns.   Unless
this Agreement otherwise requires, the covenants of this Agreement shall survive the transfer
