4842-7393-4218v2
of title.

13. Except for performance of the obligations under and enforcement of the terms and conditions
of this Agreement, the City of Cheyenne reserves all immunities and defenses provided for in
the Wyoming Governmental Claims Act, Wyo. Stat. § 1-39-101 et seq.  This Agreement shall
be governed by the laws of the State of Wyoming, and any actions relating to or arising out of
this Agreement shall be brought in the District Court of the State of Wyoming, First Judicial
District, Laramie County, sitting at Cheyenne, Wyoming.

14. It is mutually understood and agreed that Parcel A and Parcel B may be subject to easements
for public water and sewer utilities, gas and electric utilities, telecommunications utilities, and
other installations and fixtures.  The obligations of the parties with respect to easements shall
be governed by the provisions of Paragraph 4 of this Agreement relating to title and title
insurance.

15. The parties acknowledge that they and their counsel have reviewed and revised this Agreement
and that the normal rule of construction to the effect that any ambiguities are to be resolved
against the drafting party will not be employed in the interpretation of this Agreement or any
exhibits or amendments hereto.

16. Failure of any party to exercise any right given hereunder or to insist upon strict compliance
with regard to any term, condition or covenant specified herein, will not constitute a waiver of
that party’s right to exercise such right or to demand strict compliance with any term, condition
or covenant under this Agreement. This Agreement is not intended to create and does not create
a joint venture or partnership between any of the parties.

17. This Agreement constitutes the sole and entire agreement of the parties and is binding upon
the parties, their successors, legal representatives and assigns. The recitals to this Agreement
are by this reference incorporated herein. This Agreement may be executed in counterparts,
each of which may be deemed and original, and all of which will constitute one and the same
agreement.

